  "Question": "What is the mean of the data 3, 5, 7, 9, 11?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "7",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The sum is $3+5+7+9+11=35$. The mean is $35\\div5=7$.\n\nAlternative method 1: Equalize the values while preserving the total\n\nThe values balance around \\(7\\). Transfer \\(4\\) from \\(11\\) to \\(3\\), and \\(2\\) from \\(9\\) to \\(5\\); all five values then become \\(7\\). These transfers preserve both the total and the number of values, so they preserve the mean. The mean is therefore \\(7\\).",
